$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,3E)-4-[(S)-2,6,6-Trimethylcyclohex-2-enyl]but-3-en-2-ol [(S,S)-(-)- α
-ionol] 21. nBuLi (1.6M in hexane, 0.124 mL, 0.20 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was
added to a solution of sulfone 18 (50 mg, 0.18 mmol, 1 equiv) in anhyd
THF (2.0 mL) at -78 °C. After 30 min of stirring at -78 °C, a solution of
freshly prepared (S)-2-tert-butyldiphenylsilyloxypropanal37 (67 mg, 0.21
mmol, 1.15 equiv) in anhyd THF (1.0 mL) was added via canula to the
yellow solution of the anion. Stirring was continued for further 10 min
at -78 °C, then the reaction was quenched with satd aq NH4Cl (20 mL) and
extracted with Et2O (3x25 mL). The combined organic extracts were dried
over MgSO4, concd, and the residue was filtered through a short pad of
flash silica gel eluted with hexane-EtOAc 95:5. The filtrate was
evaporated and the residue was immediately submitted to the reduction
step. The crude hydroxy-sulfone 19 was dissolved in anhyd MeOH (5 mL) and
solid Na2HPO4 was added to the resulting solution. After stirring for 10
min, the mixture was cooled to -40 °C, and 1.5 equiv of solid sodium
mercury amalgam (10% Na) was added in small portions to keep the
temperature at about -40 °C. The stirred mixture was then warmed to -20
°C and stirring was continued for an additional 30 min. The excess
amalgam was filtered off and MeOH was removed. The residue was dissolved
in Et2O (30 mL) and the organic solution was washed with satd aq NaHCO3
(2x20 mL), brine, dried over MgSO4, and concd (CAUTION: compound 20 is
highly volatile). TBAF (1M in THF, 0.30 mL, 0.30 mmol, 2.0 equiv) was
added to a solution of the crude silyl ether 20 (65 mg, about 0.15 mmol,
1.0 equiv) in anhyd THF (1.5 mL) at 0 °C, and stirring was then continued
for 12 h at rt. Volatiles were removed at reduced pressure (≥mmHg;
CAUTION: α -ionol 21 is highly volatile) and the residue was purified by
silica gel flash chromatography (hexane-EtOAc 98:2) to yield
(S,S)-(-)-α-ionol 21 (27 mg, yield = 77% from sulfone 18) as a colorless
oil. (S,3E)-4-[(S)-2,6,6-Trimethylcyclohex-2-enyl]but-3-en-2-ol
[(S,S)-(-)- α -ionol] 21, yield (27 mg,77%). GC analysis revealed that
the sample was diastereomerically pure, though marred by t- BuPh2SiOH
(about 8% by GC) which could not be removed by chromatography. [α]20 D
-294.3 (c 1.0, CH2Cl2) [lit.:18 [α]20 D -293 (c 1.0, CHCl3) for a sample
showing 87% ee]; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.84 (s, 3H), 0.91 (s, 3H),
1.12-1.25 (m, 1H), 1.28 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 1.35-1.52 (m, 1H), 1.58 (br
s, 3H), 2.00 (1.96-2.06, m, 2H), 2.10 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 2.48 (br, 1H,
OH), 4.31 (quintet, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.42 (m, 1H), 5.44 (dd, J = 15.3,
8.4 Hz, 1H), 5.54 (dd, J = 15.3, 6.5 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (75.2 MHz, CDCl3) δ
22.8, 23.0, 23.5, 26.9, 27.6, 31.4, 31.9, 53.8, 69.0, 121.0, 131.3,
133.9, 135.8; EIMS m/z 194, 176, 161, 149, 138, 123, 109, 95, 91, 80, 67,
55, 43. HRMS calcd for C13H22O m/z 194.16707, found 194.16710.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, stage 2 key step is Julia-Lythgoe olefination,
intermediate from stage 5 is highly volatile
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
