$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Triethyl-hex-5-en-3-ynyloxy-sliane: To a
stirred solution of vinyl bromide (1.0 M solution of THF, 18 mL, 18.0
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (208 mg, 0.18 mmol), CuI (91.6 mg, 0.48 mmol), and Et3N
(3.4 mL, 24.0 mmol) was added a solution of but-3-ynyloxy-triethylsilane
(2.21 g, 12.0 mmol) in THF (6 mL) via a syringe pump over 1 hour. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 hours and then it
was filtered through Celite. The solvent was removed in vacuo.
Purification of residue by flash chromatography (SiO2: Rf = 0.72,
hexanes/EtOAc = 20/1) gave the enyne product.
2-Hydroxy-3-(2-triethylsilanyloxy-ethyl)-hexa-3,5-dienoic acid ethyl
ester, yield 70%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 6.54 (ddd, J = 10.2, 11.2,
16.6 Hz, 1H), 6.23 (d, J = 11.2 Hz, 1H), 5.31 (dd, J = 16.6, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
5.22 (dd, J = 10.2, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 4.38 (d, J =
5.6 Hz, 1H), 4.22 (m, 2H), 3.72 (m, 1H), 3.63 (m, 1H), 2.59 (m, 1H), 2.38
(m, 1H), 1.27 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 0.96 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 9H), 0.61 (q, J =
8.0 Hz, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 173.2, 136.2, 131.9, 131.7, 119.7,
76.0, 62.4, 61.5, 30.7, 14.2, 6.6, 4.1. HRMS Calcd. for C16H31O4Si (M+1):
315.1992, Found: 315.1987. FTIR (neat): 3503, 2955, 1732, 1459, 1240,
1189, 1085, 1017, 912, 746 cm-1. HPLC (Chiralcel OD-H column, 0.5%
i-PrOH/hexanes, 0.5 mL/min, 254 nm), tmajor = 17.3 min, tminor = 20.7
min; ee = 90%. [α]D = + 118.3 (c = 1.73, CH2Cl2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Reductive Coupling of 1,3-Enynes to Glyoxalates Mediated
