$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Allylation of
Aldehydes 2a-k. An oven-dried 50 mL round-bottomed flask was cooled under
argon and charged with (1S,2R)-(+)-2-amino-1,2-diphenylethanol (2 mmol),
indium powder (2 mmol), anhydrous THF (14 mL), anhydrous pyridine (2
mmol), and allyl bromide (2 mmol). The mixture was stirred vigorously at
25 °C for 30 min, at which time n-hexane (2 mL) was added, the solution
was cooled to-78 °C (dry ice/acetone bath), and freshly distilled
aldehyde (1 mmol) was added dropwise. After 2 h the reaction was quenched
with saturated ammonium chloride (2 mL) and allowed to warm to 25 °C .
Deionized water was added and the mixture was extracted with n-hexane (2
x 5 mL), then the combined organic layers were dried with anhydrous
magnesium sulfate, filtered through a small plug of silica gel, and
evaporated to give the alcohol product as an oil.
2-Chloro-α-(2-propenyl)benzenemethanol, 2f (Table 2, entry 6). Following
the general procedure above, 2f was obtained as a clear, colorless oil
(0.177 g, 97% yield). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.21 (s, 1H, OH),
2.34-2.46 (m, 1H), 2.61-2.71 (m, 1H), 5.18-5.24 (m, 2H), 5.81-5.97 (m,
1H), 7.19-7.36 (m, 3H), 7.57-7.60 (d, J = 7.5, 1H). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 42.0, 69.5, 118.6, 127.0, 128.4, 129.3, 131.8, 134.2, 141.1.
Enantiomeric excess was determined to be 78% by chiral GC analysis. GC
conditions: 151 °C isothermal; tR for the (R)-alcohol: 71.95 min, tR for
the (S)-alcohol: 73.27 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
