$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(2-Bromo)phenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (1g)7 Following the
Representative Procedure, 2-bromobenzaldehyde (185 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexanes/MTBE (4:1, 300 mL) provided 1g (195
mg, 86%) as a white solid 1-(2-Bromo)phenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (1g)7, yield
195 mg, 86%. Data for 1g: 1H NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.56 (dd, J = 8.0,
1.4, 1 H, Aryl), 7.52 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.4, 1 H, Aryl), 7.34 (td, J = 8.0,
1.4, 1 H, Aryl), 7.13 (dt, J = 8.0, 1.4, 1 H, Aryl), 5.94-5.83 (m, 1 H,
HC(3)), 5.24-5.16 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 5.10 (dt, J = 8.8, 3.4, 1 H, HC(1)),
