$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Treatment of 1,1-dimethylallene (1a) and SnCl2
with benzaldehyde (2a), in a mixture of aqueous hydrochloric acid and DMF
at ambient temperature in the presence of PdCl2- (PPh3)2 (2 mol %), leads
to the formation of carbonyl allylation product 3a in 95% isolated yield
(Scheme 1). The reaction is completely regioselective, giving 3a as the
sole product. Yield 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, 99:1 anti:syn
