$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of (S)-1-arylbut-3-en-1-ols (1).6 A
stirred solution of [(-)-B-chlorodiisopinocampheyl borane] (1.5 eq) in
dry THF (25 mL) was cooled to -78 °C and treated with allyl magnesium
chloride (2.0 M in THF, 1.5 eq) under nitrogen. The solution was stirred
for 1 h and allowed to warm to rt over a further 1 h. The solution was
cooled to -78 °C and treated with a solution of aldehyde (1 eq) in dry
THF (10 mL). The solution was stirred for 1 h and allowed to warm to rt
over a 1 h. The solution was treated with a pre-formed mixture of 3.0 M
sodium hydroxide (2.2 eq) and 30% hydrogen peroxide (2.5 eq). After 10
min the mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (150 mL), washed with
water (2 x 50 mL) and brine (50 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvent
evaporated under reduced pressure to yield the crude product which was
purified by flash chromatography on silica gel eluting with an increasing
proportion of ethyl acetate in hexane.
(S)-1-(2'-Chlorophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol ((S)-1e). 2-Chlorobenzaldehyde (1.41
g, 8.88 mmol) was treated according to the general procedure to yield
alcohol (S)-1e as a colourless oil (1.24 g, 77%, 94% ee): silica gel TLC
Rf0.26 (10% ethyl acetate-hexane); [α] D22 -76.1 (c 1.35, CHCl3). Chiral
HPLC (Chiralcel OD-H, 2% IPA/hexane) Rf 20.74 min (R-isomer), Rf 21.76
min (S-isomer). Spectral data as previously reported.
