$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [18O]-(±)-1-(2'-Chlorophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (16). A stirred solution of
[18O]-2-chlorobenzaldehyde (900 mg, 6.36 mmol) in dry THF (20 ml) was
cooled to -78°C under nitrogen and treated dropwise with allyl magnesium
chloride (3.81 mI, 7.63 mmol, 2.0 M in THF). The solution was stirred for
15 min and then allowed to reach rt. The solution was stirred for 2 h,
and then quenched with water (5 ml). The mixture was extracted with EtOAc
(2 x 30 ml), and the combined organic extracts were washed with brine (30
ml), and dried (MgSO4). The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
to yield the crude product which was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel eluting with an increasing proportion of ethyl acetate in
petrol from 0 to 10% to yield alcohol 16 (848 mg, 72%) as a colorless
oil; [18O]-(±)-1-(2'-Chlorophenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (16), Yield 848 mg, 72%
ca. 50% 18O as estimated by 13C NMR spectroscopy; silica gel TLC Rf 0.26
(10% ethyl acetate-petrol); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 2.16 (br, 1H), 2.38
(dt, J = 14.3, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.60-2.68 (m, 1H), 5.13-5.24 (m, 3H), 5.87
(dddd, J = 16.9, 10.4, 7.7, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.21 (td, J = 7.7, 1.8 Hz, 1H),
7.30 (td, J = 7.7, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (td, J = 7.7, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.57 (td,
J = 7.7, 1.8 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 42.08, 69.68 (18O-C),
69.70 (16O-C), 118.73, 127.07, 127.15, 128.49, 129.45, 131.78, 134.30,
141.30; FT-IR (neat) 3360, 3073, 2979, 2911, 1640, 1595, 1574, 1473,
1438, 1033, 755 cm-1; MS (CI) m/z 187 (MH+, 0.5%), 185 (MH+, 1), 183
(MH+, 1.6), 167 (37), 165 (100).
