$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-3-(2-(1-hydroxy-2-phenylethyl)phenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (11i). Benzyl
bromide (4.35 g, 25.5 mmol) was added so slowly to a mixture of Mg (645.6
mg, 26.5 mmol) in THF (30 ml) that the mixture was kept mild refluxing.
After addition, the mixture was stirred for 2 h. To a solution of
(E)-2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-enyl)benzaldehyde (10a) (1.62 g, 10 mmol) in THF
(20 ml) was added a solution of above Grignard reagent (25.5 mmol) at
room temperature. The reaction solution was stirred for 10 h under
refluxing. After the reaction was cooled to 0 °C, an aqueous saturated
solution of NH4Cl (40 ml) was added dropwise and the resulting mixture
was stirred for 10 min. The aqueous phase was extracted with diethyl
ether (30 mL × 3). The combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuum. The crude residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 1/1). Product 11i
as yellowish oil (1.80 g, 71% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.34
(br, 1H), 2.57 (br, 1H), 2.89-3.00 (m, 2H), 4.14-4.16 (m, 2H), 5.10 (dd,
J = 8.2 Hz, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 6.01 (dt, J = 15.6 Hz, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (d, J =
15.6 Hz, 1H), 7.11-7.13 (m, 2H), 7.19-7.37 (m, 5H), 7.46 (d, J = 1.2 Hz,
1H), 7.48 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 44.9, 63.3,
71.7, 125.6, 126.3, 126.4, 127.4, 127.5, 127.8, 128.3, 129.5, 131.0,
134.7, 138.2, 140.7; MS (EI) m/z (rel) 163 (20), 145 (50), 131 (50), 118
(14), 117 (100), 115 (45), 91 (37), 77 (14); HRMS for C17H18O2: 254.1307;
Found: 254.1305; IR (film): 3340 (br), 2919 (w), 1453 (w), 1004 (m), 964
(m), 755 (s), 733 (s), 698 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM crude from stage 1 added in stage 2
