$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: anti-(E)-Butyl
7-hydroxy-6,8-dimethyl-5-methylenenon-2-enoate (4a) According to the
general procedure A the catalyst was prepared from zinc iodide (32 mg,
0.10 mmol), zinc dust (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31 mg, 0.05
mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then n-butyl acrylate (0.08 mL, 0.55
mmol) and isoprenylpinacolboronic ester 1 (107 mg, 0.55 mmol) were added
to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred for 16 h. After
dilution and cooling to 0 °C isobutyraldehyde (0.05 mL, 0.50 mmol) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature for 1 h.
After quenching with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work up and
purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel,
pentane/diethylether 2:1) the desired product 4a was obtained.The dr was
determined with the signals at 6.97 and 6.82 ppm. anti-(2E,8E)-Butyl
7-hydroxy-6-methyl-5-methylenedeca-2,8-dienoate (4k) According to the
general procedure A the catalyst was prepared from zinc iodide (32 mg,
0.10 mmol), zinc dust (7 mg, 0.10 mmol) and CoBr2(dppe) (31 mg, 0.05
mmol) in 0.5 mL dichloromethane. Then n-butyl acrylate (0.08 mL, 0.55
mmol) and isoprenylpinacolboronic ester 1 (107 mg, 0.55 mmol) were added
to the reaction mixture which subsequently was stirred for 16 h. After
dilution and cooling to 0 °C (E)-crotonaldehyde (0.04 mL, 0.50 mmol) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature for 1 h.
After quenching with triethanolamine (0.08 mL, 0.55 mmol), work up and
purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel, pentane/diethyl
ether 2:1) the desired product 4k was obtained.The dr was determined with
the signals at 6.96 and 6.80 ppm. A colorless oil (130 mg, 0.49 mmol,
98%, dr 95:5). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 7.01-6.91 (m, 1H), 5.86 (d, J
= 15.5 Hz, 1H), 5.75-5.64 (m, 1H), 5.41 (ddd, J = 15.3, 7.6, 1.7 Hz, 1H),
5.00 (s, 1H), 4.91 (s, 1H), 4.13 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H), 3.88 (t, J = 7.9
Hz, 1H), 2.93 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.29-2.19 (m, 1H), 1.75 (s, 1H), 1.71
(d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 1.66-1.59 (m, 2H), 1.45-1.33 (m, 2H), 0.98-0.91 (m,
6H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 166.4, 148.3, 146.1, 131.9, 128.8,
123.1, 113.6, 75.4, 64.2, 46.9, 36.6, 30.7, 19.2, 17.7, 16.2, 13.7. IR
(film, cm-1): 3478, 3080, 2962, 2935, 2876, 1720, 1654, 1456, 1384, 1311,
1276, 1214, 1162, 1067, 1027, 989, 968, 899, 734. MS (EI): m/z = 266 (M+,
1), 248 (10), 196 (37), 175 (5), 167 (13), 159 (6), 147 (30), 140 (19),
131 (17), 119 (16), 111 (70), 95 (100), 86 (17), 79 (40), 71 (51), 55
(14). HRMS (APCI): calculated for C16H26O3H: m/z = 267.1955; found m/z =
267.1952.
