$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Nazarov reagent 17 A LDA solution was prepared by adding n-butyllithium
(1.6 M in hexanes, 0.81 mL, 1.29 mmol) to a solution of diisopropylamine
(0.2 mL, 1.41 mmol) in THF (10 mL) at 0°C. After complete addition, the
mixture was brought to -78°C and allyl acetate (0.14 mL, 1.29 mmol) was
added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 45 min at -78°C and a
solution of aldehyde 16 (251 mg, 1.17 mmol) in THF (1 mL) was added.
After stirring for 1h at -78°C, an aqueous ammonium chloride saturated
solution was introduced and the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate.
The combined organic layers were washed with water, dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate, filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
crude alcohol was directly used for the next step.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in situ prepared LDA
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Versatile Strategy to Access Tricycles Related to Quassinoids and
Triterpenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
