$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2. General procedure for the preparation of
propargylic ketones1. To a solution of trimethylsilyl acetylene (1.1
equiv.) in THF at -78 °C under Ar atmosphere, n-BuLi (1.05 equiv., 1.6 M
in hexane) was added dropwise. The mixture was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C.
The corresponding aldehyde (1 equiv.) was then added and the reaction was
stirred for additional 30 min at -78 °C. After the reaction was warmed up
to room temperature in 30 min, the mixture was quenched with water and
extracted with diethyl ether. The combined organic layers were washed
with brine, dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. K2CO3 (3 equiv.) was added to the above crude mixture in MeOH.
The reaction was allowed to stir at room temperature for 2 h. The solid
was removed by filtration through a pad of celite and washed with
dichloromethane. The filtrate was washed with aqueous ammonium chloride
and brine and dried over MgSO4. After evaporation of the solvent, the
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (VPE : VEA =
10:1 ) to afford the corresponding propargylic alcohol. Final product.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladacycle-Catalyzed Reaction of Bicyclic Alkenes with Terminal Ynones:
Regiospecific Synthesis of Polysubstituted Furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
