$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(Naphthalen-1-yl)-3-buten-1-ol (1k)8 Following the
Representative Procedure, 1-naphthylaldehyde (156 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 70 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexanes/MTBE (10:1, 100 mL; 4:1, 200 mL)
provided 1k (156 mg, 79%) as a colorless oil.
1-(Naphthalen-1-yl)-3-buten-1-ol (1k)8, yield 156 mg, 79%. Data for 1k:
1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) 8.08 (d, J = 8.2, 1 H, Aryl), 7.88 (d, J = 7.8,
1 H, Aryl), 7.80 (d, J = 8.2, 1 H, Aryl) 7.65 (d, J = 7.1, 1 H, Aryl),
7.55-7.45 (m, 3 H, Aryl), 5.98-5.90 (m, 1 H, HC(3)), 5.52 (dd, J = 8.3,
4.0, 1 H, HC(1)), 5.28-5.18 (m, 2 H, HC(4)), 2.80-2.58 (m, 2 H, H2C(2)),
2.30 (br, 1 H, HO) 13C NMR: (125 MHz, CDCl3) 139.3 (Aryl), 134.7 (C(3)),
133.7 (Aryl), 130.2 (Aryl), 128.9 (Aryl), 127.9 (Aryl), 126.0 (Aryl),
125.4 (Aryl), 125.3 (Aryl), 122.9 (Aryl), 122.8 (Aryl), 118.3 (C(4)),
69.9 (C(1)), 42.8 (C(2)) IR: (NaCl) 3560 (m), 3399 (s), 3069 (m), 2928
(m), 1639 (m), 1596 (m), 1510 (m), 1431 (m), 1394 (m), 1261 (m), 1166 (m)
MS: (CI) Calcd. for C14H15O, 199.1123; found, 199.1124 TLC: Rf 0.61
(hexanes/EtOAc, 3:1) [UV, CAM]
