$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-(1-Hydroxy-3-phenylpropyl)acrylicacid (8a).
A solution of methyl acrylate (12.4 g, 0.144 mol), hydrocinnamaldehyde 6a
(14.4 g, 0.107 mol) and DABCO (1.63 g, 14.5 mmol) was stirred at rt for
10 d. The crude reaction mixture was dissolved in MeOH (45 mL) and 2 M
KOH (125 mL) and stirred at rt for 24 h. MeOH was removed in vacuo, and
the aqueous mixture was acidified with 2 M HCl (160 mL) and then
saturated with NaCl. The mixture was then diluted with Et2O (200 mL). The
organic layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with
Et2O (3 x 150 mL). The combined organic extracts were dried (MgSO4 ),
filtered and concentrated. Purification by flash chromatography on silica
gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc 9: 1 to 4: 1 to 5:2) provided a white solid
(16.3 g, 74%). Recrystallization from toluene/hexane provided 8a as white
prisms: 2-(Hydroxy-p-tolylmethyl)acrylic acid (8h). Prepared by the
procedure described for 8a. Purification by flash chromatography on
silica gel (petroleum ether/ EtOAc 1:1) provided 8h as an off white (0.36
g, 73%):6 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.20 (m, 5 H), 6.47 (s, 1H), 5.97 (s, 1H),
5.54 (s, 1H), 2.34 (s, 3H).
