$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diethyl zinc (1.1 M in toluene, 55 μL, 0.06
mmol) was charged to an anhydrous solution of borolanes 12 and 6 (91 : 9
of borolanes 12 and 6, 300 mg, 1.8 mmol) and pmethoxybenzaldehyde (0.15
mL, 168 mg, 1.2 mmol) in toluene (6 mL) under argon at 0°C. The
homogeneous solution was agitated at 0 οC for 18 h. HPLC analysis of the
reaction solution at 18 h showed 99 : 1 site selectivity between
propargyl 5a and allenylic 4a alcohols by comparison to reference
standards of allenyl and homopropargylic alcohols.1 The reaction was
warmed to ambient temperature and treated with diethanolamine (0.35 mL).
The reaction mixture was agitated for 1 h at ambient temperature. The
reaction was diluted with isopropyl acetate (10 mL) and washed with water
(3 x 10 mL). The organic portion was concentrated to an oil. Purification
by silica gel chromatography (10-20 % EtOAc in hexanes) provided the
propargylic alcohol 5a. Allenyl alcohol 4c was prepared by the
representative procedure with o-chlorobenzaldehyde (518 mg, 3.69 mmol),
allenyl borolane 6 (994 μL, 5.53 mmol) and diethyl zinc (1.1 M in
toluene, 167 μL, 0.18 mmol) in toluene (18 mL). HPLC analysis of the
reaction mixture compared to standard references1 showed a 99 : 1 ratio
between the allenyl and homopropargylic alcohols. Purification by silica
gel chromatography (20 vol % EtOAc in hexanes) provided the intended
allenyl alcohol 4c. A colorless oil (612 mg, 92%). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.56 (dd, J = 7.8, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (dd, J = 7.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H),
7.28 (dt, J = 7.6, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.20 (dt, J = 7.7., 1.7 Hz, 1H), 5.65 (m,
1H), 5.45 (ddd, J = 6.5, 6.5, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 4.91 (dd, J = 6.6., 2.7 Hz,
2H), 2.40 (d, J = 4.4 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 207.1, 140.0,
132.1, 129.4, 128.7, 127.3, 127.1, 93.8, 78.7, 68.4. ESIHRMS C10H9ClO
calcd for [M+ H -H2O]+ 163.0320 found 163.0313.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Zinc-Catalyzed Allenylations of Aldehydes and Ketones
