$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Homoallylic Alcohol 3a: A solution of known aldehyde 21 (1.18 g, 3.49
mmol, 1 equiv) in dry Et2O (34 mL, 0.1 M) at 0 °C was treated dropwise
with allylMgBr (5.23 mL, 5.23 mmol, 1.5 equiv, 1M in Et2O) under
nitrogen. After stirring for 15 min, the reaction mixture was quenched
slowly at 0 °C with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (10 mL) and diluted with H2O
(10 mL). The layers were separated and the aqueous layer extracted with
EtOAc (3 x 10 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated under vacuum to give a colorless oil. Flash
chromatography with (20% EtOAc/Hexanes) provided homoallylic alcohol 3a.
Colorless oil, yield 1.20 g, 3.14 mmol, 90%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(ppm) = 7.68 - 7.66 (m, 4H), 7.44 - 7.36 (m, 6H), 5.81 (ddt, J = 17.5,
10.2, 7.2, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 5.55 (dq, J = 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, 8.8 Hz, 1H), 5.16 -
5.11 (m, 2H), 4.48 - 4.43 (m, 1H), 4.06 (s, 2H), 2.35 - 2.24 (m, 2H),
1.64 (s, 3H), 1.45 (d, J = 3.6 Hz, 1H), 1.09 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (150 MHz,
CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 137.28, 135.55, 134.35, 133.63, 129.65, 127.64, 125.93,
117.97, 68.05, 67.37, 42.05, 26.81, 19.27, 13.87. IR (cm-1): f = 3401,
3072, 2959, 2857, 1641, 1462, 1265, 824, 739. HRMS-ESI: M+Na = 403.2064
calculated for C24H32NaO2Si, experimental = 403.2051.
