$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: 1,1,1-Trichloroalkane (0.4
mmol) and aldehyde (0.4 mmol) in THF (1 mL) were added to a stirring,
grayish suspension of anhydrous CrCl2 (1.6 mmol) in THF (10 mL) under
argon at ambient temperature. After 10-12 h, the resultant reddish
reaction mixture was quenched with water and extracted thrice with ether,
and the combined ethereal extracts were evaporated in vacuo.
Chromatographic purification on SiO2. (Z)-chloroalkenol adducts in the
indicated yields (Table 1). 2-Chloro-1,5-diphenyl-penta-2(Z),4-dien-1-ol
(16) Melting point: 74-75°C Rf = 0.30 (hexane/ether, 7/3) IR (neat):
3342, 3015, 2901, 2875, 1630, 1594, 1494, 1452, 1310, 1082, 751cm-1 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 7.55-7.25 (m, 10H), 7.13 (dd, 1H, J = 16, 11 Hz),
6.75 (d, 1H, J= 16 Hz ), 6.70 (d, 1H, J = 11Hz), 5.41 (d, 1H, J = 5 Hz),
2.20-2.45 (d, 1H, J = 5 Hz) MS: m/z 270 (M+), 272 (M++2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chromium Vinylidene Carbenoids: Stereospecific Synthesis of
(Z)-2-Chloroalk-2-en-1-ols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Barma, D. K.; Baati, Rachid; Valleix, Alain; Mioskowski, Charles; Falck,
J. R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2001), 3(26), 4237-4238

