$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of bromobenzene (3.96 g, 2.7 mL,
25.2 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was added n-BuLi (10.0 mL, 25.2 mmol, 2.5 M
solution in hexanes) at -78 °C. After stirring at the same temperature
for 1 h, s-1a (4.88 g, 21.0 mmol in 50 mL of THF) was added. The
resulting solution was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 8 h.
Then the mixture was quenched with saturated ammonium chloride solution.
The reaction mixture was extracted with ether and dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated, and the residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 10:1).
(E)-2-Benzylidene-1-phenyl-4-( trimethylsilyl)but-3-yn-1-ol (1e). Column
chromatography on silica gel (eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl acetate =
3:1) afforded the title product. 84% yield (3.1 mmol scale, 798.7 mg) as
a brown oil. 1H NMR(400 MHz, CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 0.34 (s, 9H), 2.72 (d, J =
5.2 Hz, 1H), 5.49 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.05 (s, 1H), 7.43-7.52 (m, 6H),
7.61-7.63 (m, 2H), 8.03-8.05 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3, Me4Si) δ
-0.4, 77.4, 102.3, 105.0, 124.3, 126.6, 127.8, 128.06, 128.2, 128.6,
128.9, 134.8, 135.6, 141.7. HRMS (EI) calcd for C20H22OSi: 306.1440,
found 306.1438.
