$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the
Propargylation and Subsequent Deprotection of Aldehydes and Ketones with
Propargyl Borolane 2 Homopropargylic alcohol 6f was prepared by the
representative propargylation conditions for alkyne 6a from
2-furancarboxaldehyde (0.817 mL, 0.948 g, 9.86 mmol) and propargyl
borolane 2 (3.77 g, 93.5 wt%, 14.8 mmol) with 2 mol% diethyl zinc (1.1 M
solution in toluene, 179 μL, 0.197 mmol). Purification by silica gel
chromatography (10-25 % EtOAc in hexanes) provided the homopropargylic
alcohol 6f as a clear and colorless oil (1.30 g, 97 %). 1H and 13C NMR
spectra correspond to previously reported characterization.4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
