$DATUM 1-(4-(Trifluoromethyl)phenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (7b):
4-(Trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde (2 mmol), allyl bromide, (2.4 mmol), and
zinc powder (2.4 mmol) in 2 mL of saturated ammonium chloride solution
and 0.5 mL of THF were stirred for 2 h at room temperature. The reaction
mixture was then extracted with ethyl acetate and dried over MgSO4. The
solvent was removed under vacuum and the residue purified by flash silica
gel column chromatography using hexane and ethyl acetate as the eluents
(82 % Yield). 1-(4-(Trifluoromethyl)phenyl)but-3-en-1-ol, (82 % Yield).
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.61 (d, J= 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.48 (dd, J= 8.1, 0.5
Hz, 2H), 5.80 (d, J= 6.5 Hz, 1H), 5.21 - 5.17 (m, 2H), 4.85 - 4.75 (m,
1H), 2.61 - 2.41 (m, 2H), 2.13 (d, J= 3.3 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 147.73, 133.68, 126.08, 125.42, 125.38, 125.34, 125.31, 119.27,
72.50, 43.93. HRMS (ESI) Calculated for C11H10F3O [M-H]- : 215.06892,
Found: 215.06889.
