$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (R/S)-1-Phenylpent-4-en-1-ol (rac-15b) To the
solution of benzaldehyde (14b) (2.0 mL, 0.02 mol) in dry THF (30 mL) was
added 2 M homoallyl magnesium bromide solution in Et2O (9.8 mL, 0.02 mol)
at -78°C. Mixture was allowed to reach r. t. over 1 h and sat. NH4Cl
solution was added, followed by extraction with EtOAc. Organic phase was
separated, washed with brine and dried over Na2SO4. Product was purified
by column chromatography (EtOAc/ PE = 1/ 8),
(R/S)-1-(Naphthalen-2-yl)pent-4-en-1-ol (rac-15e) Prepared in analogy to
compound rac-15b. Yield 1.4 g (98 %), colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 1.86-2.02 (m, 3H), 2.10-2.26 (m, 2H), 4.86-4.90 (m, 1H),
4.98-5.01 (m, 1H), 5.06 (dq, J = 2.0 Hz, 17.0 Hz, 1H), 5.81-5.82 (m, 1H),
7.45-7.51 (m, 3H), 7.79-7.85 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 30.0,
37.9, 74.1, 115.0, 124.0, 124.6, 125.8, 126.1, 127.7, 127.8, 128.3,
133.0, 133.2, 138.1, 141.9. In HRMS conditions no signal observed. Data
are consistent with literature2 values.
