$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A: Formation of alcohols via allyl
indium reagents s-Butyl lithium (1.0 M solution in hexanes, 3.0 eq.) was
added to a stirred solution of allyl ethyl ether (3.0 eq.) in THF (10
mL/mmol) at -78 °C. After stirring for 1 h, a solution of InCl3 (1.0 eq.)
in THF (5 mL/mmol) was added. Stirring was continued for a further 30 min
before addition of the corresponding aldehyde (1.0 eq.). After 1 h, the
reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature before addition
of 1.0 M aq. HCl solution (5 mL/mmol). The aqueous layer was extracted
with Et2O (10 mL/mmol × 2) and the combined organic layers were washed
with water (10mL/mmol) and sat. aq. NaCl solution (10 mL/mmol) and dried
over Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the
crude product was purified by flash column chromatography to give the
corresponding alcohol as a mixture of diastereoisomers which were not
separated. (1RS,2RS) and (1RS,2SR)-2-Ethoxy-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol 6d
Benzaldehyde (102 μL, 1.00 mmol) was subjected to general procedure A and
purified by flash column chromatography (10:1 petrol:Et2O) to give
alcohol 6d as a colourless oil (172 mg, 90%) and a mixture of
diastereoisomers (ca. 4:1 from 1H NMR) which were not separated. The 1H
and 13C NMR data provided is for the major diastereoisomer. νmax (thin
film)/cm-1 3457br s, 3032s, 2976s, 2875s, 1495s, 1454s, 1399s, 1197s,
1086s, 929s, 763s, 701s; δH (400.2 MHz, CDCl3) 1.25 (3H, t, J 7.0,
C(2')H3), 3.36- 3.44 (2H, m, C(1')H, OH), 3.67 (1H, m, C(1')H), 3.72-3.77
(1H, m, C(2)H), 4.50 (1H, d, J 7.5, C(1)H), 5.07 (1H, ddd, J 17.5, 1.5,
1.0, C(4)H), 5.15 (1H, ddd, J 10.5, 1.5, 1.0, C(4)H), 5.57 (1H, ddd, J
17.5, 10.5, 7.0, C(3)H), 7.24-7.38 (5H, m, Ph); δC (100.6 MHz, CDCl3)
15.2 (C(2')), 64.5 (C(1')), 76.8 (C(1)), 85.8 (C(2)), 119.0 (C(4)), 127.4
(Ph), 127.9 (Ph), 128.1 (Ph), 134.7 (C(3)), 139.8 (i-Ph); m/z 215 (100%,
MNa+); HRMS (ESI) C12H16NaO2 (MNa+) requires 215.1043, found 215.1040
(-1.04 ppm).
