$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(4-(Trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1o)3 Following
the Representative Procedure, 4-(trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde (174 mg,
1.0 mmol), RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130
μL, 1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL,
0.1 mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal
standard for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30
psi of CO at 70 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexanes/MTBE (4:1, 250 mL) provided 1o (170
mg, 79%) as a pale yellow oil. 1-(4-(Trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-3-buten-1-ol
(1o)3, yield 170 mg, 79%. Data for 1o: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.58 (d, J
= 8.3, 2 H, Aryl), 7.45 (d, J = 8.3, 2 H, Aryl), 5.83-5.72 (m, 1 H,
HC(3)), 5.21-5.17 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 4.79 (td, J = 7.8, 4.0, 1 H, HC(1)),
2.58-2.43 (m, 2 H, H2C(2)), 2.22 (br, 1 H, HO) 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3)
147.7 (C(1')), 133.6 (C(3)), 129.7 (q, J = 32.3, C(4')), 126.1 (C(2') &
C(6')), 125.3 (q, J = 3.7, C(3') & C(5')), 124.1 (q, J = 261.6, C(7')),
119.1 (C(4)), 72.5 (C(1)), 43.8 (C(2)) IR (NaCl) 3390 (s), 3079 (m), 2982
(m), 2909 (m), 1642 (m), 1621 (m), 1417 (m), 1326 (s), 1164 (s), 1125
(s), 1068 (s), 1017 (s) HRMS (CI) Calcd. for C11H12OF3, 217.0840; found,
217.0846 TLC Rf 0.52 (hexanes/ethyl acetate, 3:1) [UV, I2, CAM]
