$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R,E)-7-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)hept-4-en-3-ol (9): A 500 mL flask was
charged with (+)-MIB (543 mg, 2.27 mmol) and 100 mL pentane and cooled to
0 ºC. A solution of Et2Zn (90.90 mL, 1.0 M in hexanes) was added,
followed by addition of aldehyde 8 (10.00 g, 45.45 mmol) in toluene (100
mL) dropwise. The reaction was stirred at 0 ºC for 7 h until alkyl
addition was complete by TLC and quenched with a saturated solution of
NH4Cl. The organic and aqueous layers were then washed with brine and
dried over MgSO4. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure
and the residue was chromatographed on silica (10% ethyl acetate in
hexanes). The (R,E)-7-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)hept-4-en-3-ol 9 (10.56 g, 93%)
as a colorless oil. Rf (hexane/ethyl acetate 9:1) 0.32; [α]25 D -1.6 (c
1.1, CHCl3); IR (film): 3418, 2934, 2860, 1613, 1586, 1463, 1248, 1095,
1035 cm-1; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.24 (d, J = 8.40, 2H), 6.86 (d, J
= 8.40 Hz, 2H), 5.62 (m, 1H), 5.51 (dd, J = 17.20, 6.84 Hz, 1H), 4.42 (s,
3H), 3.94 (m, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 3.47 (t, J = 6.76 Hz, 2H), 2.32 (m, 2H),
1.50 (m, 2H), 0.88 (t, J = 7.48 Hz, 3H); 13 C-NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3): δ
159.1, 134.7, 130.4, 129.2, 128.1, 113.7, 74.2, 72.4, 69.4, 55.2, 32.6,
29.9, 9.7; HRMS-EI (m/z) [M]+ calcd for C15H22O3 250.1569, found
250.1573.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
