$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of furan (0.5 mL, 6.9 mmol) in 10 mL of THF was treated
dropwise with n-butyllithium (4.2 mL, 1.6 M in hexane, 6.7 mmol) under an
argon atmosphere at ambient temperature for 3 h, followed by addition of
citronellal (1.0 g, 6.5 mmol) at 0 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed
to warm to ambient temperature, quenched by addition of water (5 mL),
extracted with ether (200 mL), the organic layer was separated and washed
with saturated NH4Cl solution and brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel to give a mixture of two isomer 12 (3.0 g,
91% yield, dr = 3:1). 12, Yield (3.0 g, 91%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ =
0.92 (d, J = 6.8 Hz; 3H), 1.13~1.20 (m, 1H), 1.33~1.56 (m, 2H), 1.59~1.69
(complex, 6H), 1.82~2.00 (m, 4H), 2.22 (s, 1H), 4.74 (t, J = 6.8 Hz; 1H),
5.05~5.09 (m, 1H), 6.20 (d, J = 2.8 Hz; 1H), 6.30~6.31 (m, 1H), 7.35 (m,
1H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 17.6, 19.0, 19.9, 25.2, 25.3, 25.6,
28.7, 29.1, 36.7, 37.4, 42.6, 65.5, 65.9, 105.5, 105.8, 110.0, 124.6,
131.2, 1414.7, 141.8, 156.8 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, dr = 3:1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New Metal-Free One-Pot Synthesis of Substituted Allenes from Enones
