$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-1-(Furan-2-yl)-4-(trimethylsilyl)hexa-1,4,5-trien-3-ol (11h):
Following the general procedure: to a 10 mL RBF flask was charged copper
(II) iso-butyrate (6.9 mg, 0.029 mmol, 0.025 equiv) and R,R-PhBPE (24 mg,
0.046 mmol, 0.04 equiv). The flask was sealed and then purged with argon.
To the solids were charged 4.0 mL of anhydrous tetrahydrofuran. The
resulting solution was agitated at ambient temperature for 30 min to
afford a homogeneous green solution. To the solution was charged a 1.0 M
solution of lithium tert-butoxide (0.029 mL, 0.029 mmol, 0.025 equiv).
The solution instantly turned to a dark green solution. The solution was
agitated at ambient temperature for 10 min and then cooled to -20 °C. To
the batch was charged the propargyl boronate 1a (0.442 g, 1.73 mmol, 1.50
equiv) followed by (E)-4-(furan-2-yl)but-3-en-2-one 9h (134 mg, 1.1 mmol,
1.00 equiv in 1 mL of THF). The batch was agitated at -20 °C for 15 h, at
which point HPLC analysis (220 nm) indicates complete consumption of the
ketone. 1H-NMR of the crude reaction mixture indicates 24:1 ratio of
allenyl to propargyl products. To the batch was charged 2 mL of saturated
sodium bicarbonate and 2 mL of EtOAc and the batch was stirred for 2
mins. The aqueous layer was cut and the organic layer was passed through
a silica plug. The plug was washed with 5 mL of EtOAc and the combined
organic filtrates were concentrated. The resulting material was purified
by flash silica chromatography (EtOAc/Hexanes).
(E)-1-(furan-2-yl)-4-(trimethylsilyl)hexa-1,4,5-trien-3-ol (11h), yield
231 mg, 91%; and 10h. 11h: 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ: 7.17-7.16 (m, 1H),
6.27-6.18 (m, 2H), 6.08-6.01 (m, 2H), 4.644-4.640 (m, 1H), 4.39-4.25 (m,
2H), 2.11-2.10 (m, 1H), 0.00 (s, 9H). 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 208.4,
153.2, 142.9, 130.9, 119.3, 112.3, 109.0, 100.8, 73.2, 72.1, 0.0.
