$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical reaction procedure for the intramolecular Morita-Baylis-Hillman
reactions: 1-(5-hydroxy-1-cyclopentenyl)-1-propanone (3a). 1 To a stirred
solution of 1a (105 mg, 0.75 mmol) in t-BuOH (7.5 mL) was added PPh3 (197
mg, 0.75 mmol) at 40 °C. The mixture was stirred at that temperature for
60 h, diluted with ethyl acetate, washed with water, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by flash chromatography to afford 3a (76 mg, 0.54
mmol) in 72% yield. 1-(5-hydroxy-1-cyclopentenyl)-1-propanone (3a) 1, (76
mg, 0.54 mmol) in 72% yield IR (CH2Cl2): ν 3463, 3055, 2981, 2939, 2844,
1659, 1621, 1378, 1055, 739, 704 cm-1 ; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ
1.11 (3H, t, J = 7.2 Hz, CH3), 1.81-1.87 (1H, m, CH2), 2.28-2.48 (2H, m,
CH2), 2.65-2.76 (3H, m, CH2), 3.38 (1H, s, OH), 5.13 (1H, br s, CH), 6.87
(1H, s, CH); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 7.8, 30.9, 31.3, 31.9, 75.2,
145.3, 145.4, 200.7; MS (EI) m/z (%): 140 (3.5) [M+ ], 111 (100), 93
(17.2), 83 (79.2), 67 (20.6), 55 (29.6); HRMS (EI) calcd. for C8H12O2 (M+
) requires 140.0837, found: 140.0853.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM intramolecular Morita-Baylis-Hillman reaction, use of MeCN as solvent
gave 59% yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Influence of Michael Acceptor Stereochemistry on Intramolecular
Morita-Baylis-Hillman Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Teng, Wen-Dong; Huang, Rui; Kwong, Cathy Kar-Wing; Shi, Min; Toy, Patrick
H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(1), 368-371

