$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the allenylation of
aldehydes with reagent 1R. The allenylation of n-PrCHO with 1R is
representative. A solution of 1R (1.23 g, 5.0 mmol) in EE (25 mL) was
cooled to -78 °C and a solution of n-butyraldehyde (0.46 mL, 5.0 mmol) in
EE (5 mL) at -78 °C was added to it slowly via a double ended needle.
After 3 h at -78 °C, the solvents were removed under vacuum to yield
essentially pure borinate 5a. The (1S,2S)-(+)- pseudoephedrine (0.83 g,
5.0 mmol.) and acetonitrile (15 mL) were added, and the mixture was
refluxed for 4 h. The crystals were separated and washed with
acetonitrile (2 x 3 mL) to afford 1.55 g (84%) of (+)-4R. The residue was
distilled to give 0.45g of (-)- (S)-5-hexyn-3-ol (6a) (82%).
(-)-(R)-1-(2-Furyl)-3-butyn-1-ol (6f): 80 %yield. (10R)-B-
((1S)-2-Furyl)-3-butyn-1-oxy)-10-trimethylsilyl-9-borabicyclo-[3.3.2]decane
(5f). bp 70-72 °C, 1.5 mm Hg, >98% GC/13C NMR purity, [lit.3 bp 62 °C,
0.6 mm Hg]; [α]28D = - 6.61 (2.4, MeOH); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.37-7.36 (m, 1H), 6.34-6.32 (m, 2H), 4.85 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 2.75 (dd,
J = 6.3, 2.6 Hz, 2H), 2.05 (t, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
154.6, 142.2, 110.2, 106.5, 79.9, 71.0, 65.9, 25.9. (10R)-B-
((1S)-2-Furyl)-3-butyn-1-oxy)-10-trimethylsilyl-9-borabicyclo-[3.3.2]decane
(5f): (>98% purity by 13C NMR), 1H NMR ( 300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.36 (m, 1H),
6.33-6.26 (m, 2H), 5.28 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 2.81-2.77 (m, 2H), 2.27 (m,
1H), 1.98 (t, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 1.81-1.19 (m, 13H), 0.68 (d, J = 2.3 Hz,
1H), -0.02 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 154.6, 141.8, 110.1, 106.5,
80.4, 70.1, 68.7, 33.1, 32.8, 31.5, 29.0, 27.4, 25.9, 25.8, 24.5, 22.9,
21.8, 0.6; 11B NMR ( 96 MHz, CDCl3 ) δ 55.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, enantioselective, 95% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
