$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Enone 8: To a solution of aldehyde 17 (35 mg, 0.166 mmol) in THF (2.8 mL)
at –78 °C was added an Aldrich solution of vinylmagnesium Grignard
reagent (1.0 M THF, 0.15 mL, 0.15 mmol). After 1 h the reaction was
quenched with 10 mL of saturated brine. The resulting emulsion was
diluted with EtOAc (100 mL) and the bilayer was separated. The organic
extract was further washed with water (3 x 30 mL), dried (Na2SO4),
filtered and concentrated. The crude oil was purified by SiO2 column
chromatography (3:1 hexanes/EtOAc) to furnish 33.6 mg (85% yield) of an
intermediate allylic alcohol. IR (film, NaCl) 3430, 1650, 1277, 923 cm-1;
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.82-7.77 (m, 4H), 7.58 (app t, J = 7.5 Hz,
1H), 7.53-7.46 (m, 4H), 6.04 (ddt, J = 16.0, 10.4, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 5.39 (app
dt, J = 16.0, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.28 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 1H), 5.23 (app dt, J =
11.0, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 2.30-2.10 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
196.3, 147.0, 139.7, 137.6, 138.6, 132.3, 130.3, 129.9, 128.2, 126.0,
115.9, 74.9; HRMS (CI+) m/z 239.1107 [(M+H)+; calc’d for C16H15O2:
239.1072].
