$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Dual catalysis : Tributylstannane (39 μL, 0.125 mmol, 2.5 equiv.) was
added to a mixture aldehydes (0.050 mmol, 1 equiv.) and POM 3a (10 mg,
0.020 mmol, 4.0 mol %) dissolved in 0.5 mL of DMF in a sealed microwave
vial containing a stir bar. The mixture was stirred and heated at 125 °C
under μW (120W) for 3 hours. Then, H2O2 was added and the mixture was
stirred overnight at r.t. The solvent was evaporated and the crude
material was purified by column chromatography (Petroleum ether/AcOEt:
9/1 until 7/3). The desired sulfone 8 as a colorless oil (9.3 mg, 0.041
mmol, 82% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.92 (d, 2H, J = 8.6 Hz, H
arom.), 7.57 (d, 2H, J = 8.6 Hz, H arom.), 5.88-5.73 (m, 1H, CH2-CH=CH2),
5.22-5.16 (m, 2H, CH2-CH=CH2), 4.85 (br s, 1H, CHOH), 3.05 (s, 3H,
MeSO2), 2.59-2.41 (m, 2H, CH2-CH=CH2), 2.22 (br s, 1H, CHOH). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): 140.9 (C arom.) , 137.7 (C arom.), 134.4 (CH2-CH=CH2),
126.9 (CH arom.), 126.5 (CH arom.), 118.7 (CH2-CH=CH2), 73.0 (CHOH), 43.9
(CH2- CH=CH2), 16.1 (MeSO2). HRMS calc. for C11H14O3SNa: 249.0561; found:
249.0556.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Containing Organopolyoxometalates Derived from Dawson Polyoxometalate
[P2W15V3O62]9-: Lewis Acidity and Dual Site Catalysis
