$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure D (via aldehyde 2a): The reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo and General Procedure D for the
Preparation of Adducts 4a-4c from Furfurals 2a-2c: To a flame dried
re-sealable reaction tube purged with argon and containing a magnetic
stirrer, was added (R)-Ir-complex I (20.4 mg, 0.020 mmol, 5 mol%), K3PO4
(84.9 mg, 0.400 mmol, 100 mol%), and the corresponding furfural (0.40
mmol, 100 mol%). THF (0.2 mL, 2 M concentration with respect to the
aldehyde), H2O (36 μL, 2.0 mmol, 500 mol%), i-PrOH (61 μL, 0.80 mmol, 200
mol%) and α-methyl allyl acetate (86 μL, 0.80 mmol, 200 mol%) were added
and the reaction mixture was allowed to stir at 70 °C for 48 hours. The
reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash column
chromatography (SiO2), under the conditions noted, to furnish the
corresponding products of crotylation 4a-4c. Procedure D (via aldehyde
2b): The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash
column chromatography (SiO2: pentane:Et2O, 5:1) to furnish the title
compound (52.6 mg, 79% yield, >20:1 dr, 94% ee) as a colorless oil. TLC
(SiO2): Rf (Hexane:Et2O, 5:1) = 0.09. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 6.11 (d, J
= 3.2 Hz, 1H), 5.88 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H), 5.79 (ddd, J=17.3, 10.3, 8.1 Hz,
1H), 5.17 (m, 2H), 4.31 (dd, J=8.1,3.8 Hz, 1H), 2.67 (sext, J= 7.3 Hz,
1H), 2.26 (s,3H), 2.06 (d, J=4.0 Hz, 1H), 0.92 (d, J=6.8 Hz, 3H) 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): 153.2, 151.9, 140.5, 117.1, 108.4, 106.1, 71.6, 43.7,
16.7, 13.8. RMS(CI): Calcd. for CHO (M-H)+: 165.0916, Found: 165.0916.
HRMS (CI): Calcd. for CHO (M-H)+: 165.0916, Found: 165.0916 FTIR (neat):
3414, 2965, 2924, 1219, 1017, 912 cm-1. Opt. Rot. [α]D26 = +69.1 (c =
0.58, in CHCl3) for 88% ee HPLC (Chiralcel AS-H column, Hexane:i-PrOH,
95:5, 0.5 mL/min, 210 nm): tminor= 14.2 min, tmajor= 14.9 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, dr>20:1, ee=94%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective carbonyl allylation, crotylation, and tert-prenylation
of furanmethanols and furfurals via iridium-catalyzed transfer
hydrogenation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
