$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
(1R)-3-(2,2-dimethyl-2-silapropyl)-1-(2-methyl(1,3-oxazol-4-yl))but-3-en-1-ol
(2d): A mixture of (R)-(+)-BINOL (81 mg, 0.28 mmol), 1M Ti(OiPr)4 in
CH2Cl2 (0.14 mL, 0.14 mmol), oven-dried powdered 4-Å Molecular sieves
(0.56 g), and 0.1 M trifluoroacetic acid in CH2Cl2 (43 μL, 0.0043 mmol),
in CH2Cl2 (9.0 mL) was heated at reflux for 1h. The red-brown mixture was
cooled to ambient temperature and 2-methyl-1,3-oxazole-4-carbaldehyde
(0.158 g, 1.42 mmol) was added. After stirring for 10 min the mixture was
cooled to -78°C and stannane 1 (1.20 g, 2.84 mmol) was added. The mixture
was stirred for 10 min and then placed in a -20°C Freezer for 72 h.
Saturted aqueous NaHCO3 solution (3.0 mL) was added, and the mixture was
stirred for 1 h before being transferred to a separatory funnel. The
layers were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3
× 10 mL). The organic layers were combined and washed with brine (20 mL),
dried over MgSO4, and then filtered through a plug of Celite. After
concentration under reduced pressure, the crude material was purified by
flash chromatography, eluting with 35% ethyl acetate in hexanes. Entry e,
Yield 96%. Analytical data for
(1R)-3-(2,2-dimethyl-2-silapropyl)-1-(2-furyl)but-3-en-1-ol (2e): Rf 0.26
(20% EtOAc in Hexanes); [α]D20 +11.60° (c 0.1, CHCl3); 500-MHz 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 7.38 (dd, J= 2.0, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.34 (dd, J= 3.4, 2.0 Hz, 1H),
6.27 (d, J= 3.4 Hz, 1H), 4.83 (ddd, J= 6.8, 6.8, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 4.77 (m,
1H), 4.73 (m, 1H), 2.51 (dd, J= 6.8, 1.0 Hz, 2H), 2.27 (br s, 1H), 1.55
(ABq, J= 13.7 Hz, ΔAB = 23.9 Hz, 2H) 0.05 (s, 9H).125-MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3)
δ 156.3, 143.7, 142.1, 111.3, 110.4, 106.2, 65.5, 44.8, 26.7, -1.2; IR
(neat) cm-1 3404 (br), 3075, 2954, 2897, 1634; HR CI-MS for C12H19OSi
(M+1-18) requires m/z 207.12052. Found 207.12089.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, mol. sieves used, in-situ generated catalyst
