$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
4-(2,2-dimethyl-2-silapropyl)-1-(phenylmethoxy)pent-4-en-2-ol (±2a):
Stannane 1 (0.335 g, 0.803 mmol) and benzyloxyacetaldehyde (0.107 g,
0.712 mmol) were combined with toluene (0.7 mL) and heated at reflux for
3 h. The toluene was evaporated and the crude material was purified by
flash chromatography, eluting with 20% ethyl acetate in hexanes. Yield
90%. Rt (R) (min) 80.59 ppma, Rt (S) 80.38 ppma (min).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pyran Annulation: Asymmetric Synthesis of 2,6-Disubstituted-4-methylene
Tetrahydropyrans
