$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-3-(4-pyridinyl)propanenitrile (19c). Purification
by column chromatography (1:5 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound
19c (160 mg, 99%) as a orange solid. Spectral data were identical to
those previously reported.8 TLC: R f 0.16 (1:5 hexane/EtOAc). mp: 102.6
°C. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.65 (d, 2H, J = 6.0 Hz), 7.36 (d, 2H, J =
6.0 Hz), 6.17 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz), 6.11 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz), 5.35 (s,
1H), 2.00 (brs, 1H). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 149.8, 149.6, 132.1,
125.9, 121.2, 117.0, 71.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium triflimide as solvent
gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
Applications to the Baylis-Hillman Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
