$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure D: To a flame-dried round-bottom flask equipped with a
stir bar was added 1.0 M vinylmagnesium bromide in THF (17.2 mL, 12.0
mmol) and THF (10 mL). The solution was cooled to 0 °C and
4-(trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde (1.37 mL, 10.0 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was
added dropwise via cannula. The reaction was allowed to stir at 0 °C for
2 hours. The reaction was then quenched with sat. NH4Cl (aq.) and
extracted into diethyl ether 3 times. The combined organics were washed
with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The
unpurified reaction mixture was purified on silica gel (15%
EtOAc/hexanes) to afford 1-(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol.
Light yellow oil, 1.55 g (77% yield). Rf = 0.28 (15% EtOAc/hexanes, stain
in KMnO4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
