$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. General Procedure and Products of the
Ni/Cr-Mediated Coupling A general procedure is described here for the
Ni/Cr-mediated coupling. A pear-shape flask was charged with a magnetic
stir-bar, NiCl2-CrCl3-ligand complex (9.29 mg, 0.01 mmol, 0.02 equiv),
Zr(cp)2Cl2 (Strem, 99%; 175.4 mg, 0.60 mmol, 1.2 equiv), Mn powder
(Aldrich, 99.99%; 54.9 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2.0 equiv), LiCl (Aldrich,
anhydrous, ground powder; 42.4 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2.0 equiv) and DME (Aldrich,
anhydrous, 99.5%; 1.0 mL). To the above mixture, were added aldehyde
(0.50 mmol) and iodide (0.55 mmol) under nitrogen. The mixture was
stirred at rt under nitrogen and monitored by TLC. After the reaction
proceeded to completion (usually in 2 hs), the reaction mixture was
diluted with EtOAc and Florisil was added. After stirring was continued
for 30 minutes, the solid was filtered off and the filtrate was
concentrated. Flash chromatography of the residue over silica gel, using
hexanes to hexanes-EtOAc 20:1 as eluent, afforded the coupling product as
a colorless oil.
(E)-1-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-4-methyloct-4-en-3-ol According to
the general procedure described above for the Ni/Cr-mediated coupling,
(E)-1-((tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)oxy)-4-methyloct-4-en-3-ol was obtained
as a colorless oil, yield 93%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.89 (t, J = 7.4
Hz, 3H), 1.04 (s, 9H), 1.32-1.42 (m, 2H), 1.45-1.70 (m, 7H), 1.95-2.05
(m, 2H), 3.67 (t, J = 6.1 Hz, 2H), 3.97-4.02 (m, 1H), 7.34-7.44 (m, 6H),
7.63-7.69 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.3, 135.8, 134.1, 129.8,
127.8, 126.9, 78.0, 64.2, 37.2. 31.8, 29.8, 29.1, 27.1, 22.9, 14.1, 11.5;
HRMS (ESI) m/z 433.2542 ([M+Na]+ calcd for C26H38NaO2Si: 433.2533).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Air-Stable Heterobimetallic Catalysts to Effect Ni/Cr-Mediated Couplings
with a ca. 1:1 Molar Ratio of Coupling Partners at Low Catalyst Loadings
