$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure 1: Preparation of allenyl
vinyl alcohols A saturated aqueous solution of ammonium chloride (0.7
mL/mmol) was added to a methanolic (2.2 mL/mmol) solution of
1-bromo-2-butyne (1.1 equiv) and the α,β-unsaturated aldehyde (1 equiv),
and the solution was cooled to 0°C. Indium powder (100 mesh) (1.1 equiv)
was added in four portions (over 20 min), and the mixture was stirred
vigorously until completion of the reaction (1 h) as evidenced by TLC.
The mixture was diluted with an equal volume of Et2O, and this was washed
with brine. The brine was re-extracted with Et2O. The combined extracts
were dried with anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated. Column chromatography
(SiO2) of the residue was carried out with 10% ethyl acetate in hexanes.
(E)-4-Methyl-1-(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)hexa-1,4,5-trien-3-ol (4f)
Following General procedure 1, p-trifluoromethyl-trans-cinnamylaldehyde15
(1.9 g, 9.7 mmol), indium powder (1.2 g, 11 mmol), and 1-bromo-2-butyne
(1.0 mL, 11 mmol) gave 4f (2.2 g, 91%) as a colorless oil: IR (film)
3384, 1960, 1616, 1327 cm-1; 1H NMR δ: 7.57 (2H, d, J = 8.3 Hz), 7.48
(2H, d, J = 8.3 Hz), 6.68 (1H, d, J = 15.9 Hz), 6.32 (1H, dd, J = 15.9,
6.4 Hz), 4.89 (2H, dq, J = 3.1, 3.1 Hz), 4.71 (1H, m), 2.22 (1H, br, OH),
1.75 (3H, t, J = 3.1 Hz); 13C NMR δ: 204.8, 140.1, 132.4, 129.6, 129.5
(q, J = 33 Hz), 126.7 (2C), 125.5 (2C, q, J = 3.6 Hz), 124.1 (q, J = 270
Hz), 101.3, 77.8, 73.0, 14.6; 19F NMR δ: -63.6; HRMS (ESI): 277.0811,
[C14H13F3ONa]+ requires 277.0816.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
