$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for methyl 4-iodobenzoate
arylations: Under nitrogen to a 25 mL round bottom flask (flame dried
under vacuum), Li(acac) (24 mg, 0.23 mmol, 0.25 eq), methyl
4-iodobenzoate (524 mg, 2.0 mmoL, 2.2 eq), and NMP (1.5 mL) were added
sequentially. This mixture was cooled to 0 °C and diethylzinc (115 μL,
1.1 mmoL, 1.2 eq) was added dropwise. The mixture was stirred for 18 h at
0 °C. A solution of (S)-1 (89 mg, 0.18 mmoL, 20 mol %) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL)
was transferred to the mixture. This was stirred 1 h at 0 °C. The
solution was warmed to room temperature for 15 m and then cooled back to
0 °C. An aldehyde (0.91 mmoL) was added and the reaction was monitored by
TLC. Upon completion of the reaction, ammonium chloride (saturated, aq.)
was added to quench the reaction. Dichloromethane was used to extract the
mixture three times. The organic fractions were dried over Na2SO4,
concentrated and the residue was purified by silica gel flash column
chromatography using hexanes (or petroleum ether)/ethyl acetate as the
eluent (0% to 12% ethyl acetate) to give product alcohol as either an oil
or solid in 52 to 97% yield. Methyl 4-(cyclohexyl(hydroxy)methyl)benzoate
(E)-methyl 4-(1-hydroxy-3-phenylallyl)benzoate 90% yield, 87% ee. 1H-NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.99 to 8.02 (d, 2H), 7.46 to 7.48 (d, 2H), 7.21 to
7.37 (m, 5H), 6.63 to 6.68 (d, 1H), 6.28 to 6.33 (dd, 1H), 5.38 to 5.40
(d, 1H), 3.89 (s, 3H), 2.96 (bs, 1H). 13C-NMR (300 MHz CDCl3) δ 166.9,
147.7, 136.0, 131.1, 130.7, 129.7, 129.1, 128.5, 127.8, 126.5, 126.0,
74.5, 52.0. [α]D25=+8.2 (c=1.075, THF) 87% ee. HPLC: chiralpak AD column;
solvent ratio: 98:2 hexanes:isopropanol, flow rate: 1 mL/min. tminor=
108.0 min, tmajor= 128.8 min. Anal. Calcd. for C17H16O3: C, 76.10; H,
6.01. Found: C, 76.29; H, 6.00. HRMS calcd. for C17H16O3: 268.1099
([MOH]+= 251.1070). Found: 251.1072.
