$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Grignard Addition to
γ-Sulfenyl Enals 7c. Freshly prepared Grignard reagent (1 M solution in
Et2O, 0.2 mmol) was added to a solution of γ-sulfenyl enal 7c (0.1 mmol)
in THF (1 mL) at -78°C. After being stirred for 2 h, the reaction mixture
was diluted with Et2O and washed with water. Evaporation of the solvent
and filtration of the residue through a short silica gel column. Mixture
of 9 and10. 9 (R1 = t-Bu, R2 = R3 = Ph, less polar alcohol, major isomer,
liquid). 9 (R1 = C(CH2)5, R2 = Ph, R3 = Me, liquid). 1H NMR δ 7.42-7.40
(m, 2H), 7.33-7.26 (m, 3H), 5.55 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 5.03-4.97 (dd, J =
15.8, 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.24-4.18 (quintet, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 1.81-1.68 (m,
6H), 1.50-1.37 (m, 4H), 1.15 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR δ 137.7, 135.3,
132.6, 131.9, 128.7, 128.2, 68.9, 53.7, 36.02, 35.97, 25.9, 23.1, 22.6;
HRMS calcd m/z for C16H22OS 262.1391, found m/z 262.1376.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Do the Electronic Effects of Sulfur Indeed Control the π-Selectivity of
γ-Sulfenyl Enones? An Investigation
